menuconfig FAULT_INJECTION
	bool "Fault injection test hooks"
	default n
	help
	  Enables FI_POINT() hooks throughout the tree. Intended for
	  test/CI builds only -- see FAULT_INJECTION_RELEASE_GUARD below.
	  When disabled, FI_POINT() compiles to exactly the wrapped call:
	  no fault-injection code exists in the binary at all, not merely
	  a disabled check.

	  This is the Zephyr adapter for the portable fault-injection core
	  (see the repo root's README.md); the registry itself
	  (src/fault_inject.c) is RTOS-agnostic, and this Kconfig only
	  covers what the Zephyr build integration needs.

if FAULT_INJECTION

config FAULT_INJECTION_MAX_POINTS
	int "Maximum number of distinct fault injection points"
	default 32
	help
	  Fixed-size table capacity for the fault registry. No dynamic
	  allocation is used, so this bounds RAM use deterministically.

# Enforcement of "must not ship in a non-test build" is a CMake-time
# FATAL_ERROR in adapters/zephyr/CMakeLists.txt, not here -- a Kconfig
# bool can express a default, but it cannot fail a build on its own, and
# a help-text-only promise is not a guard. Same rationale as C-MSP.

endif # FAULT_INJECTION
